# ============================================================================
# FlowAblation / 1D two-phase Stefan problem  (Hydro2, ablation.on = 1, ablation.conduction = 1)
#
# As input_1D_Stefan, but the solid conducts: part of the gas heat flux goes into heating the
# solid and only the rest removes it.  Gas at rest at T_inf = 1 (k_g 4.861e-3, alpha_g 1.389e-3)
# fills x > 0.5; solid (rho_s 1, cp_s 3.5, k_s = k_g -> alpha_s = alpha_g) starts at
# T_s0 = 0.985; ablation temperature T_a = 0.99 (below the contact temperature 0.9925, so the
# surface ablates from t = 0), Q* = 0.08.  Similarity solution, s = 2 lam sqrt(alpha_g t):
#   k_g (T_inf - T_a) exp(-lam^2)/((1 + erf lam) sqrt(pi alpha_g t))
#     - k_s (T_a - T_s0) exp(-lam^2 r)/(erfc(lam sqrt r) sqrt(pi alpha_s t)) = rho_s Q* lam sqrt(alpha_g/t)
#   r = alpha_g/alpha_s   ->  lam = 0.0872   (0.195 without in-depth conduction)
#   solid  T = T_s0 + (T_a - T_s0) erfc((0.5 - x)/(2 sqrt(alpha_s t)))/erfc(lam sqrt r)
# Measured (400 cells): recession -0.1 ... +0.4 %, net flux within 0.5 %, temperature
# profiles 0.13 % (gas), 0.01 % (solid) of the temperature difference.
#
# Run (from bin/): mpirun -np 4 ./hydro2-2d-g++ ../tests/FlowAblation/input_1D_Stefan2 plot_file=<dir>/output
# Check:           python3 ../tests/FlowAblation/reference/solid_conduction_check.py stefan2 <dir>
# ============================================================================
